        "title": "Clues in the Rocks",
        "reading": "The strongest evidence for evolution lies in stone. Fossils are the preserved remains of ancient life: bones, teeth, shells, and footprints turned to rock. They appear in layers, with the oldest at the bottom. By reading the layers, scientists read the history of life.\n\nThe most telling fossils are the transitions. Archaeopteryx had feathers and wings like a bird but teeth and a bony tail like a dinosaur. Tiktaalik had fins and a neck, a fish learning to walk. Whales carry tiny hip bones, leftovers from ancestors that walked on land. Each one is a snapshot of change in progress.\n\nThe fossil record is incomplete, like a book with missing pages, but the pages we have tell a clear story. Simple sea life appears first, then fish, then land animals, then mammals. New fossils keep filling the gaps, and every one fits the pattern evolution predicts.\n\nNew transition fossils appear almost every year. In China, feathered dinosaurs keep blurring the line between reptile and bird. In Africa, ancient human fossils keep pushing our own story deeper in time. The book of stone keeps gaining pages, and with each page the story of evolution grows clearer and harder to doubt. The evidence keeps piling up.",
